    {
      "id": "e27ba865-16f0-42fb-826e-68c1ec25f70a",
      "name": "Workflow overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1740,
        -720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 680,
        "height": 1280,
        "content": "## Generate scientific illustrations from research prompts with SciDraw AI\n\n[SciDraw AI](https://sci-draw.com/) turns text prompts into publication-ready scientific illustrations. This workflow creates a durable generation job through the public SciDraw REST API, waits or polls until the job reaches a terminal state, and downloads the generated image into n8n.\n\n### Who is it for?\n\nResearchers, educators, science communicators, medical writers, journal teams, and automation builders who need repeatable diagrams for manuscripts, presentations, protocols, and teaching materials.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Configure the illustration prompt, aspect ratio, resolution, and image count.\n2. Create a SciDraw image-generation job with safe idempotency.\n3. Use bounded waiting, then poll queued or processing jobs every five seconds.\n4. Stop with the public API error if a job fails or is canceled.\n5. Download the first successful result as binary data.\n\n### Setup\n\n1. Create an API key at [SciDraw API Keys](https://sci-draw.com/settings/api-keys).\n2. Give it the `images:generate`, `jobs:read`, and `credits:read` scopes.\n3. In n8n, create an **HTTP Header Auth** credential.\n4. Set the header name to `Authorization` and value to `Bearer sd_your_key`.\n5. Select that credential in both SciDraw API nodes.\n6. Update the example prompt and execute the workflow.\n\n### Requirements and cost\n\n- n8n\n- A SciDraw AI account and scoped API key\n- 5 credits per 2K image or 20 credits per 4K image\n\n### Customize\n\nReplace the Manual Trigger with a Form, Webhook, spreadsheet, Airtable, CMS, or research database trigger. Connect the downloaded image to Google Drive, S3, Notion, email, or a manuscript pipeline. Adjust the aspect ratio and resolution in one place.\n\nAPI reference: [SciDraw AI API documentation](https://sci-draw.com/docs/api)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b42edbc9-37fc-43b1-a19f-490fe8615cba",
      "name": "Request and polling notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -760,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 1. Configure and create the job\n\nEdit the request fields, then create a SciDraw job. The API key stays in n8n Header Auth credentials and is never embedded in this workflow. `Prefer: wait=30` often returns a completed result immediately, while the polling branch handles longer jobs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4dfa182f-527c-45ae-b63d-20205ae9c10c",
      "name": "Result handling notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        100,
        -180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 2. Handle the result\n\nSuccessful jobs download the first generated image as binary data. Failed or canceled jobs stop with the sanitized public API message. Queued and processing jobs wait five seconds, read the job again, and loop until terminal."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
